        "NEVER print, return or embed raw image data: no base64, no 'data:image/...' strings, no savefig-into-a-string tricks. Any matplotlib figure is captured and displayed automatically - just draw it (plt.plot(...) / plt.show()) and, if you want, print nothing. Do NOT use IPython.display / display(Image(...)) and do NOT hand-roll a savefig-into-BytesIO round-trip: no manual encoding is needed and it hides nothing, it only wastes your turn. A value you print is shown as plain text, so a base64 dump only spams the user's screen.",
