          'Decide honestly whether this picture would really show readable writing - a label, packaging, a shop sign, a title, a street sign, a screen or a piece of paper with words on it.',
          'Most pictures show NO writing at all: never add writing to a picture that does not truly need it, and never turn a plain object into a labelled product just to have some text.',
          'If the picture genuinely shows writing, write the real wording that such a thing really carries, in the correct real language of the object and its country of origin, correctly spelled with real accents, in CAPITAL LETTERS.',
          guidance,
